{
  "name": "Repost your evergreen social posts every week with Airtable and Socialync",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nGood posts should not be used once. Every Monday this workflow takes the evergreen post in your Airtable table that was posted the longest time ago, or never, and schedules it again with Socialync. It then writes the date and the number of times posted back to the record, so the next week picks a different post. You decide what counts as evergreen by ticking a box. Socialync's API has no per post results yet, so you choose the evergreen posts in your table.\n\nPosts are scheduled without a manual approval step. You can cancel or change any scheduled post in Socialync until it goes out.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create an API key at https://socialync.io/go/n8n-node-keys and add it as a Socialync credential.\n2. Add an Airtable token credential.\n3. Make a table with these fields: Caption, Platforms, Image URL, Evergreen (checkbox), Last Posted (date), Times Posted (number), Notes.\n4. Choose the base and the table in all three Airtable nodes.\n5. Tick Evergreen on a few records and connect your platforms in Socialync.\n\n### Customization\nChange the day and time in the trigger node. Change the platforms and the delay in Settings.\n\nAPI reference: https://socialync.io/go/n8n-node",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 600
      },
